[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'All right, guys. So, today we\'re going to be talking about a product that combines two of my favorite ways to listen to music. Now, when I\'m sitting at my desk, I usually prefer to use a pair of IEMs, but obviously that\'s going to be wired into an amp. But, I love the'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'convenience of true wireless earbuds, so having Bluetooth, being able to use that on the go, I always kind of go to that whenever I\'m away from the house. But, the product we\'re going to check out today, which is the brand new Moondrop'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Evo 2, basically combines both of those. It allows you to use IEMs wirelessly. It\'s ear hooks that have Bluetooth adapters built into them, and it makes everything extremely convenient. Now,'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this is coming in at $99, and we\'ve seen some products like this before, but this one is the most feature-rich of all of those type of products that I\'ve tested before. And, coming from Moondrop, which has turned into be one of my favorite'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'audio companies, this is just definitely one that I wanted to check out. So, I do want to point out what this is. If you\'re not familiar with this type of product, let\'s say that you prefer listening to IEMs. Again, those give you much better sound than most true'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wireless earbuds, but they usually rely on being plugged into an amp because they need things to just bring out the power a little more, bring out the lows, the mids, and the highs, just amplify it. And, again, that\'s why it needs an amplifier. But, what the Evo does is it'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gives you the ear hook design, and it has all of that built in to the ear hook. So, it doesn\'t need to be plugged into anything. The IEMs just plug in straight into these adapters, which are using the two-pin connection.'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It does say that later they are going to release the MMCX connector as well. But, as of right now, it\'s just the two-pin connector. And, here are some of the features that it has. So, it is Bluetooth 6.0. They do use a custom Moondrop chip in'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these. It also allows you to use the online interactive DSP, which is basically where other users have uploaded uh equalizers that they have set by using this product. Uh it kind of'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gives you flexibility and it just lets you use what other ones have found to work for them. Again, you can use your own because there is a 10-band equalizer uh that you can use within the app, which that\'s another plus. Uh this'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'product allows you to connect to Moondrop\'s app and gives you some pretty good functionality. It even gives you a gaming mode, so uh if you want to switch into a gaming mode and not have to worry about lag, you have that option. This also has some very high-end Bluetooth'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'codecs that it\'s compatible with. It even has uh LHDCV, which is allowing you to use these at up to 24-bit playback, so you\'re getting really high-end audio that way. Uh it'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also supports LDAC playback, which I feel is huge. And it also supports LE audio or low energy audio. Uh this allows you to, you know, get really good performance and not have to sacrifice uh'

[02:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as much battery life. So, it\'s not as power-hungry as some of these other ones, which LDAC and LHDCV is definitely going to drain your battery uh a little bit more than what LE audio will do. Uh and then another huge feature is it also'

[03:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uses a class D amp chip in here. Uh so, that\'s a lot going on and a lot that they\'ve had to cram into these little ear hooks. Now, the first thing I want to point out uh as far as accessories that it comes with and obviously it\'s'

[03:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very important here is the case. The case on here is huge. Uh it kind of reminds me of like the Pelican cases that, you know, you carry around camera gear. Uh but this is with a purpose. You kind of have to think, if you\'re'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plugging an IEM into this, you need enough room cuz some IEMs are huge. Uh so, you you know, you got to have room for that. This case is crush-proof and it\'s also coming in rated at IPX7, so it\'s waterproof as well. So, if you do'

[03:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
